Subject: [PATCH 02671/11362] [outer-loop] Qwopus-27B Q3_K_M Layer-B +
 events-to-solve + Kaggle engine clarification

Qwopus-27B-Coder Q3_K_M (13.5GB, fits 16GB) grounds 1/2 (ka59 129tok/46s; tn36 RAMBLED 1086tok/468s) --
SAME as the small Qwen3.5-9B/Qwen3-14B/Phi-4 but 1.5-2.4x bigger + slower. Answer to operator: quantizing
a 27B down does NOT beat the small Q4 reasoners on this rule-induction task.

Events-to-solve (the metric that matters for per-step ARC + ARC-AGI-3 efficiency): Phi-4 grounds in 52tok,
Qwen3-14B 188tok, vs gemma 586-607 -- the stronger reasoners reach the answer in 3-11x fewer events; gemma
grounds reliably but is the most verbose.

Kaggle engine: NOT transformers-only. llama-cpp-python+CUDA runs offline via a bundled prebuilt wheel
(Kaggle Dataset, pip --no-index) -- GGUF benchmarking transfers. transformers is the fallback (bigger fp16
KV -> tighter). Two must-verifies: (1) the prebuilt CUDA wheel offline in a real Kaggle notebook; (2) the
REAL per-GPU VRAM -- ARC Prize runs L4x4 (24GB ea) or T4x2 (16GB ea); at 24GB a 27B Q4 fits a single L4 and
the 'too big' conclusion flips. The 16GB figure is a working assumption.

